&lt;p&gt;The Server assigns ids, timestamps and versions, validates input and applies
PATCH; the &lt;code&gt;Backend&lt;/code&gt; keeps what it is given and enforces what only it can see:&lt;code&gt;ErrConflict&lt;/code&gt; for a taken &lt;code&gt;userName&lt;/code&gt; (409 &lt;code&gt;uniqueness&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;InvalidValue&lt;/code&gt; for a
member that does not exist (400 &lt;code&gt;invalidValue&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;ErrPrecondition&lt;/code&gt; when the
stored version is not the one that was read. &lt;code&gt;NewMemory()&lt;/code&gt; is the reference
implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It serves &lt;code&gt;/Users&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/Groups&lt;/code&gt; (list with &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;startIndex&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;count&lt;/code&gt;,&lt;code&gt;attributes&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;excludedAttributes&lt;/code&gt;; create; get, &lt;code&gt;PUT&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PATCH&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DELETE&lt;/code&gt; by
id with &lt;code&gt;ETag&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;If-Match&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;/Users/.search&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/Groups/.search&lt;/code&gt;, and the
discovery endpoints &lt;code&gt;/ServiceProviderConfig&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/ResourceTypes&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/Schemas&lt;/code&gt;.Filters cover the whole grammar of RFC 7644 §3.4.2.2; PATCH is atomic: an
operation that fails leaves the resource as it was.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-it-refuses-and-why"&gt;What it refuses, and why&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-it-refuses-and-why"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-it-refuses-and-why" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Everything here comes from outside, so the limits are part of the API:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a body over &lt;code&gt;MaxBodyBytes&lt;/code&gt; (1 MiB), a PATCH with more than &lt;code&gt;MaxOperations&lt;/code&gt; (100), or one that grows the resource past the body limit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;413&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a group with more than &lt;code&gt;MaxMembers&lt;/code&gt; (10 000)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;400 &lt;code&gt;invalidValue&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a filter over 4 KiB, nested deeper than 32, with an unknown operator, or &lt;code&gt;gt&lt;/code&gt; on a boolean&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;400 &lt;code&gt;invalidFilter&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;writes to &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;meta&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;schemas&lt;/code&gt; or a user&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;groups&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;400 &lt;code&gt;mutability&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a resource without its core schema, a &lt;code&gt;userName&lt;/code&gt; that is empty, over 256 bytes or has control characters, two primary emails&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;400&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a missing or wrong bearer token (&lt;code&gt;BearerAuth&lt;/code&gt;, constant time; an empty token admits nobody)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;401&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;any Backend error that is not one of the sentinels&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;500 with a body that says nothing; the error goes to &lt;code&gt;ErrorLog&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not supported&lt;/strong&gt;: bulk operations, sorting, password changes, &lt;code&gt;/Me&lt;/code&gt;
(announced as such in &lt;code&gt;/ServiceProviderConfig&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-it-is-checked-against"&gt;What it is checked against&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-it-is-checked-against"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-it-is-checked-against" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What identity providers really send&lt;/strong&gt;, tested with their payloads: Entra
ID&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;Replace&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;, its string booleans (&lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;active&amp;quot;: &amp;quot;False&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;), its member removal
by value list, its filtered add that creates an email; Okta&amp;rsquo;s replace without a
path that repeats the &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;. The filter, PATCH and the whole handler are fuzzed(&lt;code&gt;FuzzFilter&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;FuzzPatch&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;FuzzServer&lt;/code&gt;), and the coverage lane&amp;rsquo;s floor is 92%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="reference"&gt;Reference&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="reference"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#reference" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/go-authn/scim@v0.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;pkg.go.dev/github.com/go-authn/scim@v0.1.0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>